## Pure rational case cuts · `sec:cas:decision-cuts`

**Rule (Exact cut coordinate inventory)** · `rule:cas:decision-cut-coordinates`

`Cas::check_case_cut(&CaseCut,&mut Budget)` checks whether a rational box lies in an existing native association and its case domain. `CaseCut` retains exact function and association handles, ordered `CoordinateInterval` records and an optional `IntegerCellRange`. Coordinates are distinct closed Real or Integer declarations under the exact case header; an Assignments box includes every declared Real and Integer coordinate. Integer endpoints must be integral and ordered, ensuring a nonempty lattice interval; fractional endpoints refuse instead of rounding. Reversed intervals, missing axes, foreign handles, changed headers and an association absent from the function refuse (`test:integration:integer-coordinate-cut-boxes`), (`test:integration:decision-cut-identities-and-boxes`). This pure check retains no proof authority (`rule:cas:decision-cut-lifecycle`).

**Rule (Exact mixed affine cut grammar)** · `rule:cas:decision-cut-grammar`

The checker reconstructs dense affine coefficients for rational literals, coordinates, explicit `IntegerEmbed`, negation, addition, subtraction, multiplication by a constant and division by a nonzero constant. Sign-directed extrema retain strict boundaries, equality and nonzero; affine Integer ranges compare the exact lower and upper differences. This proves mixed floor boxes for both nonnegative and bounded indices (`test:integration:integer-coordinate-cut`), while original nonlinear Integer operands still refuse (`test:integration:integer-coordinate-cut-nonlinear`). Total Boolean and native region constructors use conservative whole-box truth; a union succeeds when one member covers the box. Explicit embeddings preserve operand sorts (`rule:cas:integer-case-results`), and cut success supplies no projected family cover (`ex:cas:integer-case-family-boundary`).

**Example (Mixed cut ownership boundaries)** · `ex:cas:integer-coordinate-cut-costs`

The nonnegative, bounded `[0,5)` and parameter-bounded mixed floor boxes cost 21,214/59,680, 27,574/61,500 and 39,686/74,532 Work/staged bytes respectively. Literal `N`/`N−1` tests retain prior Work, leave graph occupancy unchanged on success or exhaustion, and succeed with zero output and retained-payload capacity (`test:integration:integer-coordinate-cut-boundaries`). Parameter boxes check both Integer endpoints over every supplied assignment (`test:integration:integer-coordinate-cut-parameters`); no cache or proof is published (`rule:cas:decision-cut-lifecycle`).

**Rule (Integral rational case cut)** · `rule:cas:decision-cut-integer`

An integer-cell question requires an `Integer`-sorted rational arm literal n, membership of n in the supplied exact integer range, and `n <= lower <= upper < n+1` on the named Real coordinate. Missing range endpoints are exact absent bounds. An integral Real arm refuses with `DecisionIntegerRange`; the case result keeps its declared Integer sort (`test:integration:decision-cut-integer-result`), (`rule:cas:integer-case-results`). The checked finite partition interface authenticates the declared option/range association before a cut is reused under that contract (`rule:cas:decision-partition-integer`).

`DecisionBoundaryIntersection` reports a box without uniform established membership; `DecisionOutsideRegion` reports uniform exclusion. Malformed boxes and option/range mismatches have distinct typed codes. Unsupported predicates, named provenance, nonlinear syntax, variable divisors, placements and non-rational cuts return `UnsupportedCertificate`. An exact separating lemma for a non-rational boundary remains unsupported by this subset. A finite radius or inward-rounded endpoint has no enclosure authority here; the missing enclosure-origin checker must establish that the original target belongs to the supplied box.

**Rule (Pure case-cut lifecycle)** · `rule:cas:decision-cut-lifecycle`

The operation leaves graph occupancy unchanged on success and refusal, returns no witness or hypothesis, and uses no cache. It charges its own traversal and exact arithmetic on the caller's cumulative ledger, retaining spent Work on refusal. The input box and dependency plan reserve staged bytes before allocation. Completed coefficient vectors reserve their measured rational payload, while one new vector and bounded scalar scratch reserve the component-ceiling bound; retained graph and output bytes are zero. The existing formal register, primitive manifest, wire format and ordinary selection route are unchanged. Certified local introduction and portable replay are separate consumers of these prerequisites (`rule:cas:decision-partition-authority`), (`def:cas:decision-introduction-contract`).

Independent cut fixtures cover integer cells (`test:integration:decision-cut-integer-cell`), all three sign regions (`test:integration:decision-cut-sign-regions`), the upper-left chart and owned real axis (`test:integration:decision-cut-phase-chart`), affine cancellation and coordinate extrema (`test:integration:decision-cut-affine-predicates`), unsupported certificates (`test:integration:decision-cut-unsupported-certificates`), exact identities and box shape (`test:integration:decision-cut-identities-and-boxes`), scope and domain (`test:integration:decision-cut-scope-and-domain`) and the read-only lifecycle (`test:integration:decision-cut-read-only-lifecycle`).

