Work and staging cover traversal, total affine reconstruction, exact cuts, cell ownership and retained copies. Returned and caller-retained bytes are the same bound; added graph bytes and reuse output are zero. Reuse staging includes the retained contract plus the full current box-cut scratch (`rule:cas:decision-partition-reuse`). These thresholds are conservative accounted bounds, not allocator measurements. Literal N/N−1 tests pin admission Work, staging, output and Cartesian cells, prior Work and one retained input byte (`test:integration:decision-partition-resource-boundaries`); reuse Work, staging and cumulative exhaustion (`test:integration:decision-partition-reuse-boundaries`); and combined admission/reuse with atomic refusal and a widened box (`test:integration:decision-partition-atomic-lifecycle`). No permanent test searches a byte threshold, and spent Work remains spent on refusal.

**Definition (Closed rational enclosure contract)** · `def:cas:decision-enclosure-contract`

`nrz_cas::decision::RationalEnclosure` names the original `target`, exact `context`, that context's actual `input_family`, rational `lower` and `upper`, and an `EnclosureOrigin`. `ExactRational { expression, value }` proposes an exact rational result; `PiBound { expression, certificate }` supplies the independent constant theorem of (`rule:cas:pi-machin-certificates`). Both require the identical original expression. `ScalarKernel` carries the scoped closed law records of (`rule:cas:scalar-kernel-certificate`). `Cas::check_rational_enclosure` returns the same sealed `CheckedRationalEnclosure` retaining the complete contract, constant theorem dependency where applicable, and logical ownership bound. Context identity remains part of the contract even though a closed target needs no input assumption (`test:integration:decision-enclosure-qualified-family`).

**Rule (Closed original-expression replay)** · `rule:cas:decision-enclosure-replay`

The checker delegates to `ExactConstant::from_expression`, which inspects every original operand, establishes finite-real divisor domains before normalization and independently checks equality to the normalized result. `ExactRational` requires an exactly rational result equal to its candidate; exact cancellation such as `Pi/Pi` needs no constant bound (`test:integration:decision-enclosure-named-constant-boundary`). `PiBound` independently validates the finite Machin certificate, or cites its byte-identical store-local judgment under (`def:cas:pi-bound-cache`), and propagates closed rational intervals through normalized negation, addition, subtraction, multiplication, division, integer powers and the checked square-root extension of (`rule:cas:constant-square-root-enclosures`); every interval divisor must exclude zero (`test:integration:decision-pi-closed-targets`). Both routes check containment in the requested box, with no floating comparisons (`rule:cas:pi-machin-certificates`).

**Rule (Closed replay refusals)** · `rule:cas:decision-enclosure-refusals`

Foreign replay handles, another target and a false rational result refuse (`test:integration:decision-enclosure-original-target`); reversed or excluding boxes refuse (`test:integration:decision-enclosure-false-boxes`); substituting a wider input family refuses (`test:integration:decision-enclosure-qualified-family`). Empty scalar records, `MatrixKernel` and `Unverified` origins return `UnsupportedCertificate` at their respective checkers (`test:integration:decision-enclosure-unsupported-origins`), (`test:integration:kernel-origin-baseline`). A hidden zero divisor remains `RefutedDomain` even under multiplication by zero or quotient cancellation (`test:integration:decision-enclosure-hidden-domain`). Free inputs, including a canceled free input, remain unsupported (`test:integration:decision-enclosure-free-input-boundary`); the scalar checker separately refuses a nominal singleton offered for a varying coordinate on `[1,2]` (`test:integration:decision-kernel-nominal-coverage-refuses`).

**Rule (Closed enclosure authority)** · `rule:cas:decision-enclosure-authority`

The sealed enclosure checks the supported closed target on the exact retained family; it establishes neither family nonemptiness nor context consistency. Alone it creates no witness, local frame, hypothesis or portable proof, and cannot connect a closed target to a separate case coordinate (`test:integration:decision-enclosure-no-membership-authority`). A separate `DecisionIntroduction` requires exact source equalities and a complete partition before introducing certified membership (`def:cas:decision-introduction-contract`). The admitted π remainder theorem is independently checked; free-input interval arguments and matrix origins remain unsupported (`rule:cas:pi-machin-certificates`), (`test:integration:decision-enclosure-unsupported-origins`). Closed scalar records retain the same limited prerequisite authority (`rule:cas:scalar-kernel-certificate`).

