## Rational endpoint enclosures · `sec:cas:rational-enclosures`

**Definition (Validated interval arithmetic)** · `def:cas:enclosure-intervals`

`enclosure::Interval` owns canonical ordered rational endpoints. Its constructor refuses reversal; addition, subtraction, multiplication, reciprocal, absolute value and maximum compute exact endpoint relations and round outward to a declared dyadic grid. Signed floor and ceiling preserve negative endpoints and exact grid points. A reciprocal refuses every zero-containing interval. Intersection requires compatible subject and premises from its caller and refuses an empty result; an interval by itself asserts neither an expression's range nor a context hypothesis. Component, intermediate, exponent and Work ceilings apply before arithmetic, including grid construction (`test:unit:enclosure-grid-integer-oracle`), (`test:unit:enclosure-arithmetic-extrema-oracle`), (`test:unit:enclosure-interval-refusals`).

**Definition (Original enclosure requests and reports)** · `def:cas:enclosure-requests`

`EnclosureRequest` names the original target and context, an ordered box of distinct free coordinates, and a width, at-most, strict-less-than or equality goal. The box restricts the queried domain; it supplies no global hypothesis. Version-one `RefinementPolicy` declares absolute precision, grid and round ceilings, analytic term and binary-reduction ceilings and Work reserved for independent checking. Supported grammar metadata is derived at expression admission so unsupported original families and impossible initial schedules refuse before evaluation Work. Original operands still undergo independent domain checking, including a divisor hidden by multiplication by zero. The current grammar is rational literals, free real, rational or integer coordinates, negation, ordered addition, subtraction, multiplication and division, and strict-real half powers with a literal exponent; two nested half powers express a fourth root under (`rule:cas:enclosure-root-grid`). The closed `NaturalLog` operator adds positive real logarithms under (`rule:cas:enclosure-log-atanh`); an opaque call name grants no logarithm semantics. The closed `Exponential` operator adds real exponentials under (`rule:cas:enclosure-exp-taylor`). The closed `Sigmoid` operator adds the logistic composition under (`rule:cas:enclosure-sigmoid-compose`), and `Tanh` adds the hyperbolic composition under (`rule:cas:enclosure-tanh-compose`). The closed `PositivePower` operator adds strictly positive bases with bounded literal rational exponents under (`rule:cas:enclosure-positive-power`). The remaining analytic families remain unsupported (`test:unit:enclosure-zero-work-preflight`), (`test:unit:enclosure-original-domain-refusals`).

**Rule (Checked decisions and stopping)** · `rule:cas:enclosure-outcomes`

